# Intentionally empty, and committed on purpose.
#
# `pnpm gen` passes this file to `wrangler types --env-file`, which *replaces* the
# default `.env` / `.dev.vars` loading. That keeps the committed
# worker-configuration.d.ts identical for every developer: it describes the bindings
# declared in wrangler.jsonc and nothing about anyone's local machine.
#
# Runtime values (DATABASE_URL, ORIGIN, BETTER_AUTH_SECRET, ADMIN_EMAILS) do not belong
# here. They are read through `$env/dynamic/private`, which is intentionally untyped,
# and are supplied locally by `.env` and in production by `wrangler secret put`.
#
# Do not add variables to this file.
